meta-rzg3l-fast-logo
====================

Seamless boot logo for the RZ/G3L SMARC EVK. U-Boot brings up the MIPI DSI ->
ADV7535 -> HDMI pipeline and shows a still image. The kernel inherits the
running pipeline instead of re-initialising it, so the image stays on screen
from a few hundred milliseconds after reset until the compositor draws its
first frame.

The layer changes the display path only. Combine it with
meta-rzg3l-fast-boot-base to shorten the boot as well.

Tested with Yocto scarthgap, RZ/G3L BSP v1.0.0, u-boot 2024.07 and
linux-renesas 6.12.46-cip8, MACHINE = "smarc-rzg3l", core-image-weston.


I. What this layer changes
==========================

  U-Boot (recipes-bsp/u-boot/)
    0001  enable CONFIG_VIDEO for smarc-rzg3l
    0002  add drivers/video/rzg2l: CPG, DSI D-PHY, DSI link, ADV7535, DU and
          VSPD are programmed from init_sequence_r, and the image is scanned
          out from 0x58000000 through a self-looping VSPD display list
    0003  load the image from /boot on the rootfs partition; keep the display
          running on a blank frame if the load fails
    0004  wait for two output frames instead of a fixed second

  Image (recipes-graphics/rzg3l-boot-logo/)
    installs boot_img_720p.bin.gz and boot_img_1080p.bin.gz into /boot

  Kernel (recipes-kernel/linux/)
    0001  reserve 0x58000000..0x5fffffff (no-map) and move the CMA pool to
          0x70000000, so nothing overwrites the frame buffer or the display
          lists during boot
    0002  add "renesas,seamless-boot-logo" to the VSPD, DU, DSI and ADV7535
          nodes
    0003  keep the MIPI DSI and LCDC module clocks running
    0004  vsp1: take over the running pipeline
    0005  rz-du: inherit the CRTC left running by U-Boot
    0006  rzg2l_mipi_dsi: inherit the running DSI link
    0007  adv7511: keep the HDMI output configured by U-Boot
    0008  adv7511: pin the connector to U-Boot's display mode
    0009  adv7511: stop the connector poll from turning the HDMI output off
    fast-logo.cfg  disable fbdev emulation, the framebuffer console and the
          kernel logo, so that the compositor makes the first DRM commit


II. Required layers
===================

A standard RZ/G3L VLP project (RZ/G3L Linux Start-up Guide, chapter 2) plus
this layer:

  poky/meta
  poky/meta-poky
  poky/meta-yocto-bsp
  meta-openembedded/meta-oe
  meta-openembedded/meta-python
  meta-openembedded/meta-multimedia
  meta-arm/meta-arm-toolchain
  meta-arm/meta-arm
  meta-renesas/meta-rz-bsp
  meta-renesas/meta-rz-distro
  meta-rz-features/meta-rz-codecs
  meta-rz-features/meta-rz-graphics
  meta-rzg3l-fast-logo

  Combining with meta-rzg3l-fast-boot-base
  ----------------------------------------
  The two layers are independent and can be used together or separately.
  Both patch r9a08g046l48-smarc.dts, in different places. Put
  meta-rzg3l-fast-boot-base first in bblayers.conf: both layers have
  priority 20, so their kernel patches are applied in bblayers.conf order,
  which is the tested order.

  meta-rzg3l-fast-logo-intro cannot be used together with this layer.


III. Build
==========

  $ source poky/oe-init-build-env build
  $ bitbake-layers add-layer ../meta-rzg3l-fast-logo
  $ bitbake core-image-weston

No DISTRO setting is required; the layer works with rz-vlp and with
rz-vlp-fast from meta-rzg3l-fast-boot-base. conf/layer.conf adds
rzg3l-boot-logo to IMAGE_INSTALL. Set RZG3L_BOOT_LOGO_PACKAGE = "" in
local.conf to build an image without the logo files.

Check the build result:

  $ strings tmp/deploy/images/smarc-rzg3l/fip.bin | grep boot_img
  ext4load mmc 0:2 0x48000000 boot/boot_img_720p.bin.gz

  $ fdtget tmp/deploy/images/smarc-rzg3l/r9a08g046l48-smarc.dtb \
        /soc/display@10890000 renesas,seamless-boot-logo


IV. Flashing
============

The logo is shown by U-Boot, which is part of fip, not of the rootfs. After
any change to this layer's U-Boot patches, write the new bl2 and fip to the
board (RZ/G3L Linux Start-up Guide). Writing only the WIC or rootfs does not
update U-Boot.

The U-Boot banner does not change between builds. To confirm that the new
U-Boot is running, check for these lines on the serial console:

  62697 bytes read in ... ms
  Uncompressed size: 3686400 = 0x384000
  DU Init
  VCPD Init for DL


V. Changing the image or the resolution
=======================================

The image file is a raw ARGB8888 frame buffer, gzip compressed. Its
uncompressed size must be exactly width * height * 4. U-Boot does not check
the geometry.

DISPLAY_MODE in drivers/video/rzg2l/rzg2l_video.c (U-Boot patch 0002) selects
the display timings and the file that is loaded. It must match the CEA VIC
set on the ADV7535 node by kernel patch 0008:

  MIPI_DSI_720P   ->  renesas,seamless-boot-logo-vic = <4>
  MIPI_DSI_1080P  ->  renesas,seamless-boot-logo-vic = <16>

If the two do not match, the kernel reports one mode while the hardware
scans out another.


VI. Known limitations
=====================

  - The hand-over is declared statically in the device tree. If U-Boot does
    not start the display (old fip, unsupported boot medium), the kernel
    still skips its own initialisation and the display stays dark until the
    compositor starts. U-Boot patch 0003 keeps the display running even when
    the image cannot be loaded, which covers the common case.

  - The HDMI connector is pinned to one mode and always reports connected.
    EDID is not read.

  - The BSP U-Boot environment has loadaddr=0x58000000, which is the logo
    frame buffer. A manual "ext4load mmc 0:2 - <file>" or "tftp <file>" at
    the U-Boot prompt overwrites the image. Give an explicit address.

  - The 128 MiB region at 0x58000000 stays reserved after the kernel has
    taken the display over.
